.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt NSS_DNSSD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nss_dnssd
.Nd host name lookups through the mDNSResponder DNS cache
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
NSS module sends unicast DNS address and reverse lookups to
.Xr mDNSResponderPosix 8
through
.Fn DNSServiceQueryRecord .
The daemon shares cached answers between processes.
The module does not maintain a separate cache.
It implements
.Xr getaddrinfo 3 ,
.Xr gethostbyname2 3 ,
and
.Xr gethostbyaddr 3 ,
including IPv4 and IPv6 addresses.
.Pp
To opt in, add
.Ql dnssd
before
.Ql dns
in the hosts database entry in
.Pa /etc/nsswitch.conf :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
hosts: files dnssd [NOTFOUND=return] dns
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Ql NOTFOUND=return
action makes negative answers from the daemon terminal.
Unavailable and temporary failures continue to
.Ql dns .
Keep
.Ql dns
as a fallback for daemon failures and unsupported lookups.
The default system configuration is not changed by installing this module.
The daemon must be running before lookups can use its cache.
.Pp
The module reads the search list and
.Cm ndots
setting from
.Xr resolv.conf 5
and submits absolute query names to the daemon.
Names under
.Ql .local
are left to other NSS sources, including the existing
.Ql mdns
source when configured.
If a search candidate is under
.Ql .local ,
the entire lookup is deferred to preserve search order.
The
.Ql dnssd
source does not replace the multicast
.Ql mdns
source.
.Pp
A and AAAA requests run concurrently, with independent completion states.
A completed address family can succeed even if the other family fails.
The polling loop uses a five second deadline per search candidate.
The DNS-SD client library performs its own synchronous request setup;
that setup can take longer than the reply deadline when the daemon stalls.
A daemon sending incomplete IPC messages can also extend processing
beyond that deadline.
.Sh LIMITATIONS
The current POSIX daemon reads IPv4 upstream nameserver addresses only.
This does not prevent resolving AAAA records through those servers.
Resolver configuration reloads can retain previously configured servers;
restart the daemon after changing upstream DNS servers.
The daemon does not implement every libc resolver option.
.Pp
The DNS-SD API reports both nonexistent names and missing record types as
.Dv kDNSServiceErr_NoSuchRecord .
The module returns
.Dv NS_NOTFOUND
for both cases.
.Pp
For security, privileged processes defer to other sources if
.Ev DNSSD_UDS_PATH
is set, since the DNS-SD client library otherwise uses that variable to
select the daemon socket.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/run/mDNSResponder
.It Pa /etc/nsswitch.conf
NSS source configuration.
.It Pa /etc/resolv.conf
Resolver search policy and daemon upstream server configuration.
.It Pa /var/run/mDNSResponder
Default daemon IPC socket.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr getaddrinfo 3 ,
.Xr gethostbyaddr 3 ,
.Xr gethostbyname2 3 ,
.Xr nsswitch.conf 5 ,
.Xr resolv.conf 5 ,
.Xr mDNSResponderPosix 8
